<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

[Appica UI](https://appica.dev/ui) components for Rails: rendered with **Phlex 2**, styled with
Appica's **Tailwind v4** classes and made interactive with **Stimulus**. Each component keeps
the compound structure of the React original, so the Appica docs map one to one.

## Components

The pages follow Appica's sidebar categories.

### Actions & Inputs

- [Autocomplete](<%= page_path(:autocomplete) %>): a text input that suggests matching options as you type.
- [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>): the trigger and action element used across components.
- [Button Group](<%= page_path(:button_group) %>): buttons joined into one control, sharing variant and size.
- [Checkbox](<%= page_path(:checkbox) %>): a tick box with a mixed state, groups and "select all".
- [Chip](<%= page_path(:chip) %>): a compact pill for tags, filters and removable tokens.
- [Combobox](<%= page_path(:combobox) %>): pick from a list filtered by typing - single, chips or creatable.
- [Copy Button](<%= page_path(:copy_button) %>): copies text to the clipboard and confirms with a check.
- [Field](<%= page_path(:field) %>): a label, description and error wired to one control, with native validation.
- [Form builder](<%= page_path(:form_builder) %>): model-bound components through `form.ui` (text, number, select, text area, check box, switch, radio and check box groups, combobox, slider, OTP), with Active Record, nested forms and validation errors.
- [Text field](<%= page_path(:input) %>) (`Input`): a single-line text field with icons, adornments and a clear button.
- [Number Field](<%= page_path(:number_field) %>): a numeric input between steppers that formats its value.
- [OTP Field](<%= page_path(:otp_field) %>): a one-time code entered one character per slot.
- [Radio](<%= page_path(:radio) %>): a set of mutually exclusive options.
- [Rating](<%= page_path(:rating) %>): a score input from a row of stars or any icon, with fractional values.
- [Select](<%= page_path(:select) %>): a button that opens a list of options to pick one or several.
- [Slider](<%= page_path(:slider) %>): a value or a range along a track, with a tooltip.
- [Switch](<%= page_path(:switch) %>): an on/off toggle for settings that apply right away.
- [Textarea](<%= page_path(:textarea) %>): a multi-line text field sharing Input's variants, sizes and slots.
- [Toggle](<%= page_path(:toggle) %>): a two-state button that stays pressed.
- [Toggle Group](<%= page_path(:toggle_group) %>): a row of toggles, single- or multi-select.
- [Toolbar](<%= page_path(:toolbar) %>): a strip of controls with one tab stop and arrow-key focus.

### Data Display

- [Avatar](<%= page_path(:avatar) %>): a user image with a text or icon fallback when it's missing.
- [Badge](<%= page_path(:badge) %>): a small label that highlights a status, count, or category.
- [Card](<%= page_path(:card) %>): a flexible content container for a title, description, media, and actions.
- [Collapsible](<%= page_path(:collapsible) %>): a section that expands and collapses to show or hide its content.
- [Separator](<%= page_path(:separator) %>): a thin horizontal or vertical line between sections, in seven styles.
- [Sparkline](<%= page_path(:sparkline) %>): a compact interactive chart for showing a trend at a glance.
- [Thumbnail](<%= page_path(:thumbnail) %>): a compact image or icon tile for file, list and media rows.

### Menus

- [Context Menu](<%= page_path(:context_menu) %>): a menu of actions for an object, opened by right-clicking it.
- [Dropdown Menu](<%= page_path(:dropdown_menu) %>): a menu of actions opened from a button.
- [Menubar](<%= page_path(:menubar) %>): a bar of menus for an app's top-level commands.

### Navigation

- [Breadcrumb](<%= page_path(:breadcrumb) %>): where the current page sits in a hierarchy, as a trail of links.
- [Navigation](<%= page_path(:navigation) %>): links between pages or sections, with the current one highlighted.
- [Navigation Menu](<%= page_path(:navigation_menu) %>): site navigation whose items open rich panels of links.
- [Pagination](<%= page_path(:pagination) %>): page links for a long list, with a truncated range builder.
- [Table of Contents](<%= page_path(:toc) %>): an "on this page" sidebar that follows the headings in view.
- [Tabs](<%= page_path(:tabs) %>): several panels sharing one region, one shown at a time.

### Overlays

- [Alert Dialog](<%= page_path(:alert_dialog) %>): a dialog that demands a response, for high-stakes confirmations.
- [Dialog](<%= page_path(:dialog) %>): a focused task or content in a centered modal, with nested dialogs.
- [Drawer](<%= page_path(:drawer) %>): a panel that slides in from a screen edge, with swipe-to-dismiss and snap points.
- [Popover](<%= page_path(:popover) %>): rich, interactive content floating beside a control.
- [Preview Card](<%= page_path(:preview_card) %>): a rich preview of a link, shown on hover or focus.
- [Tooltip](<%= page_path(:tooltip) %>): a short hint for a control, with a shared provider.

### Status & Feedback

- [Alert](<%= page_path(:alert) %>): a prominent, in-page message that draws attention to a status or event.
- [Loader](<%= page_path(:loader) %>): an indeterminate indicator for section- and status-level waits.
- [Meter](<%= page_path(:meter) %>): a graphical display of a numeric value within a known range.
- [Progress](<%= page_path(:progress) %>): the completion status of a task that takes a while, as a bar or a ring.
- [Skeleton](<%= page_path(:skeleton) %>): a placeholder block shown while content loads, with a shimmer or pulse.
- [Spinner](<%= page_path(:spinner) %>): a spinning indicator for compact, in-place waits.
- [Toast](<%= page_path(:toast) %>): a brief, dismissible notification that stacks in a corner of the screen.

### Icons

- [Icons](<%= page_path(:icons) %>): ~5,000 Appica icons drawn by name with `Icon(:star)`.

### Blocks

Ready-made compositions of the primitives, `include Blocks` to use them.

- [Chat assistant](<%= page_path(:chat_assistant) %>): an assistant chat card with suggestions, a composer and Turbo Stream replies.
- [Revenue summary](<%= page_path(:revenue_summary) %>): a revenue card with a trend badge, top markets, a chart and key stats.
- [Team members](<%= page_path(:team_members) %>): members with roles and presence, a seat count and an invite-by-email form.
- [Order tracker](<%= page_path(:order_tracker) %>): a shipment card with status, delivery progress, a step timeline and the courier.
- [Review summary](<%= page_path(:review_summary) %>): the average rating with stars, the breakdown per star and social proof.
- [Command menu](<%= page_path(:command_menu) %>): a command palette with search, grouped commands, shortcuts and keyboard navigation.
- [Music player](<%= page_path(:music_player) %>): a now-playing card with a seek bar, play / pause, skip, shuffle and repeat.
- [Newsletter](<%= page_path(:newsletter) %>): an email signup with perks, validation, a spam honeypot and social links.
- [Product card](<%= page_path(:product_card) %>): a product with a discount badge, wishlist toggle, size picker, quantity and Add to cart.
- [Transactions](<%= page_path(:transactions) %>): recent income and spending with filter tabs, icon tiles and signed amounts.

## Usage

Include the `UI` kit in any Phlex view and call components like JSX tags:

```ruby
class FrameworkPicker < Phlex::HTML
  include UI

  def view_template
    Autocomplete(items: [ "Next.js", "Remix", "Astro" ]) do
      AutocompleteInput(placeholder: "Search a framework")
      AutocompleteContent do
        AutocompleteEmpty { "No frameworks found." }
        AutocompleteList { |item| AutocompleteItem(value: item) { item } }
      end
    end
  end
end
```

From ERB: `<%%= render FrameworkPicker.new %>`.

## Conventions

- **Render props become blocks.** Appica's `{(item) => …}` render functions are blocks with an
  argument (`AutocompleteList { |item| … }`). Where Appica takes `render={<Button />}`, the part
  yields its attributes: `DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger) { "Open" } }`.
- **`className` is `class:`.** Your classes are merged with the defaults through tailwind_merge,
  so conflicting utilities (`h-14` vs `h-10`) replace them.
- **Events instead of callbacks.** `onValueChange`, `onOpenChange`, … are Stimulus events such as
  `ui--autocomplete:change` and `ui--drawer:open-change`, with the value in `event.detail`.
- **One folder per component.** Ruby parts, the Stimulus controller, CSS and the Lookbook preview
  live together in `app/components/ui/<component>/`.
